# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored — never commit real secrets.
# The orchestrator loads this file, so keys here reach the agent CLI it launches.

# --- AI backend / provider keys ---------------------------------------------
# Only needed when you run a NON-Claude backend (agent.backend / --backend). The
# wrapped CLI reads its own provider key from the environment; put it here so the
# orchestrator passes it through. Set only the one(s) your backend uses.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=            # OpenAI Codex CLI, aider (OpenAI models)
# GEMINI_API_KEY=            # Google Gemini CLI  (or GOOGLE_API_KEY)
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=         # aider/others targeting Claude via API (not Claude Code)
# For LiteLLM-backed CLIs (e.g. aider), any LiteLLM-supported provider var works.

# --- GitHub access ----------------------------------------------------------
# Used by the org orchestrator (scripts/org.py) to list an org's repos and to
# clone private ones. A classic or fine-grained token with repo read scope.
# Public orgs work without it, but you'll hit tighter rate limits.
# GITHUB_TOKEN=

# --- GitHub Enterprise Server (self-hosted GitHub) --------------------------
# Enterprise orgs are listed via <host>/api/v3 and their repos are usually
# private. A token here is OPTIONAL: if you leave these unset, org listing falls
# back to `gh auth token` and then git's credential store — the same creds
# `git clone` uses — so it authenticates wherever a single-repo clone already
# does. Set a token below only to override that. Resolution, first match wins:
#   1. GITHUB_TOKEN_<HOST>   (host upper-cased, non-alphanumerics -> _)
#   2. GHE_TOKEN / GITHUB_ENTERPRISE_TOKEN   (any non-github.com host)
#   3. GITHUB_TOKEN / GH_TOKEN               (fallback)
#   4. gh CLI token, then git credential store   (automatic, no env needed)
# For https://github.example.com/... use either of:
# GITHUB_TOKEN_GITHUB_EXAMPLE_COM=
# GHE_TOKEN=
# Optional: override the API root if it isn't <host>/api/v3.
# GITHUB_API_URL=https://github.example.com/api/v3
